  "_excluded": {
    "body": "below f0 the reference carries the source's own gain modulation rather than a body: at 7 of 9 notes the energy the metric reads is one line at f0 minus 125 or 250 Hz (-50 to -58 dB re the fundamental), the lower sideband of a gain update every 8 ms that every partial carries, and at note 48 a 50 Hz hum line (-67.8 dB). Notching those lines moves the reading from -50/-55 to -57\u2026-80 dB; they sit at no harp string's pitch and at no fixed frequency (60-273 Hz across the grid)",
    "tnr": "everything the metric counts as noise in the reference is modulation sidebands of the partials - 100 % of the non-tonal power lies below 1 kHz, in lines at f0 +- 5 Hz (-36 to -44 dB, a 5.0 Hz amplitude modulation at every note) and at n*f0 + k*125 Hz (-52 to -58 dB). Against the recordings' real floor (-93 to -105 dB per bin) the ratio would read 71-78 dB, not the 35-50 recorded, so a bound here would hold the model to the source's synthesis"
